{"content":[{"c":["OPHEL"],"sourceClass":"h1","t":"p"},{"c":["1. Hill or mound in Samaria where Elisha’s house stood (",{"href":"?bref=2Kgs.5.24","r":"2Kgs.5.24","rawR":"2Kgs.5.24","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"2Kgs.5.24","value":"2Kgs.5.24"}],"t":"ref","v":"2 Kgs 5:24"},")."],"sourceClass":"list","t":"p"},{"c":["2. Fortification in the southeast portion of ancient Jerusalem high above the slopes of the Brook Kidron, strengthened by Jotham (",{"href":"?bref=2Chr.27.3","r":"2Chr.27.3","rawR":"2Chr.27.3","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"2Chr.27.3","value":"2Chr.27.3"}],"t":"ref","v":"2 Chr 27:3"},") and Manasseh (",{"href":"?bref=2Chr.33.14","r":"2Chr.33.14","rawR":"2Chr.33.14","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"2Chr.33.14","value":"2Chr.33.14"}],"t":"ref","v":"33:14"},"). Isaiah described the destruction of such a fortress when prophesying the judgment of God upon Jerusalem (",{"href":"?bref=Isa.32.14","r":"Isa.32.14","rawR":"Isa.32.14","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Isa.32.14","value":"Isa.32.14"}],"t":"ref","v":"Is 32:14"},"). After the exile, the temple servants lived there and repaired its walls (",{"href":"?bref=Neh.3.26-27","r":"Neh.3.26-27","rawR":"Neh.3.26-27","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Neh.3.26-27","value":"Neh.3.26-27"}],"t":"ref","v":"Neh 3:26-27"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=Neh.11.21","r":"Neh.11.21","rawR":"Neh.11.21","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Neh.11.21","value":"Neh.11.21"}],"t":"ref","v":"11:21"},"). Josephus states that it was near the temple. Archaeological excavations at the traditional site in Jerusalem reveal fortifications dating from pre-Israelite times to the Maccabean period."],"sourceClass":"list","t":"p"}],"format":"bsb-study-dictionary-v2","id":"Ophel","provenance":{"archiveSha256":"10758ea00dbea7540f9337e43e59c8e4000295c1261e3426bab6f31c31dcff5b","release":"1.6","sourceCitationReferences":[{"anchorText":"2 Kgs 5:24","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=2Kgs.5.24","rawQueryValue":"2Kgs.5.24","sourceRefExact":"2Kgs.5.24"},{"anchorText":"2 Chr 27:3","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=2Chr.27.3","rawQueryValue":"2Chr.27.3","sourceRefExact":"2Chr.27.3"},{"anchorText":"33:14","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=2Chr.33.14","rawQueryValue":"2Chr.33.14","sourceRefExact":"2Chr.33.14"},{"anchorText":"Is 32:14","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Isa.32.14","rawQueryValue":"Isa.32.14","sourceRefExact":"Isa.32.14"},{"anchorText":"Neh 3:26-27","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Neh.3.26-27","rawQueryValue":"Neh.3.26-27","sourceRefExact":"Neh.3.26-27"},{"anchorText":"11:21","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Neh.11.21","rawQueryValue":"Neh.11.21","sourceRefExact":"Neh.11.21"}],"sourceItemFragmentSha256":"81f4c66617e5d49757383f2da3da9e34d8c34792c27339bfa74b4d4ddea7cb83","sourceItemName":"Ophel","sourceItemOrder":65,"sourceMember":"Articles/O.xml","supplementPointersNotIncludedAsContent":[]},"sourceAttributes":{"name":"Ophel","product":"TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","typename":"Article"},"sourceTitleExact":"Ophel","title":"Ophel","version":"v2-a101d843a2f0cd3fc0c6"}